id: pm-todos-irjt
title: Propagate the docstring gate entry guard fix
description: "The isMainInvocation entry guard swallowed realpathSync ENOENT and returned false, causing npm run docstring to exit 0 having scanned nothing — a mandatory release gate reporting success without doing its job. Propagate the throw instead so a broken environment fails loudly."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: docstrings,gate
created_at: "2026-08-10T05:47:12.408Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-21T09:18:45.171Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-21T09:16:38.321Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-21T09:16:38.321Z"
author: pi-agent
release: 2026.8.10
resolution: The mandatory docstring gate now fails loudly on an unresolvable entry and handles symlinked entry/module URLs.
expected_result: "The mandatory docstring gate executes a real repository scan, fails on broken entry resolution, and canonicalizes symlinked entry/module paths."
actual_result: Current npm test passes the four entry-guard cases and npm run docstring performs a non-vacuous repository scan.
fixed_version: 2026.8.10
notes[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T05:47:15.206Z",pi-agent,"Defect: isMainInvocation caught realpathSync ENOENT and returned false, so the top-level selector called the no-op placeholder instead of main. npm run docstring exited 0 having scanned nothing — a mandatory release check reporting success without doing its job."
  "2026-08-10T05:47:15.725Z",pi-agent,"Fix: removed the try/catch so realpathSync propagates. An unresolvable argv[1] means the environment is broken after Node already loaded this file, and a broken environment must not silently satisfy a gate. The JSDoc now documents @throws and corrects the inverted fails-closed language."
  "2026-08-10T05:47:16.117Z",pi-agent,"Verification: npm test passes (136 tests), npm run docstring exits 0 (4 files, 55 declarations), npm run coverage meets thresholds, and node --experimental-strip-types confirms isMainInvocation throws ENOENT on an unresolvable argv[1] instead of returning false."
  "2026-08-10T06:43:40.940Z",pi-agent,"Greptile (P2 on pm-beads) and CodeRabbit (Major on pm-slack) independently flagged the one-sided comparison in isMainInvocation: pathToFileURL(realpathSync(entry)).href === moduleUrl resolves only argv[1], leaving moduleUrl holding the symlink under --preserve-symlinks. Canonicalising both sides through realpathSync fixes it. Verified by measurement: with moduleUrl holding the symlink path, both-sides (new) returns true while one-sided (old) returns false."
  "2026-08-10T07:20:20.796Z",pi-agent,"The previous symlink test (isMainInvocation resolves a symlinked entry path to the real module URL) passed argv[1] as the link and moduleUrl as the REAL path, which the old one-sided comparison pathToFileURL(realpathSync(entry)).href === moduleUrl also satisfied — it could not distinguish the fixed implementation from the broken one. Added a new test (canonicalizes a symlinked moduleUrl, as --preserve-symlinks produces) that puts the symlink in moduleUrl (pathToFileURL(link).href), which is what Node records in import.meta.url under --preserve-symlinks. Verified by measurement: reverting to the old one-sided comparison makes the new test fail (fail 1), restoring the canonicalization makes it pass (fail 0). The existing symlink test is retained because argv[1] arriving through an npm bin shim is a separate real case."
tests[1]{command,scope,timeout_seconds,note}:
  npm run docstring,project,60,Real analyzer execution and declaration coverage
docs[2]{path,scope,note}:
  "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/pull/44",global,Merged implementation and review record
  "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/releases/tag/v2026.08.10",global,First release containing the gate repair
close_reason: "Merged in PR #44, shipped in v2026.08.10, and reverified against current source and defeat tests"
body: ""
